Third-party material
====================

This project was written from scratch, but its wire-format knowledge comes
from other people's work:

* qfenix -- https://github.com/iamromulan/qfenix -- BSD-3-Clause.
  The EFS2 packet field layouts, the item-file interface and several
  hard-won details (POSIX open flags, the int16 mode fields, the PUT
  response offsets) were transcribed from its diag.c and diag.h.
  Note that this project does NOT follow qfenix's opcode numbering; see
  README.md for why.

* libopenpst -- https://github.com/openpst/libopenpst -- the classic EFS2
  opcode numbering, which is what shipping modems agree with.

* QCSuper -- https://github.com/P1sec/QCSuper -- GPLv3 -- and MobileInsight's
  diag_revealer, for documenting how DIAG works on Android. Their /dev/diag
  container framing and their DIAG_IOCTL_SWITCH_LOGGING argument-probing
  technique were reimplemented in earlier versions of this helper; that
  transport has since been dropped in favour of DIAG over QRTR. No code was
  copied.
